**Key idea:** Two numbers form a pair if they have the same digit sum. Walk the array once, keep `count[s]` = how many earlier numbers had digit sum `s`; when a new number with sum `s` arrives, it pairs with all of them, so add `count[s]` to the total and then increment. O(n · d) time where d is the digit count. Use a 64-bit total, because the count can reach n(n−1)/2.

